	CDC to PDP-12 and PDP-12 to CDC communications.

I.  At the CDC, communication is implemented by programs COM2 and
COM3, which are found in the library file LIB1.  When this file has
been purged from disk, it must be copied from tape P96, using the 
following JCL:
	REQUEST,LIB1,*PF.
	REQUEST,TAPE,VSN=P96,E,NORING.
	SKIPF,TAPE,5,17.
	COPYBF,TAPE,LIB1.
	RANDOM,LIB1.
	CATALOG,LIB1,RP=30.

II.  PDP-12 to CDC-6400 communication is accomplished by the COM2
programs.  The information to be transmitted should be put in a file
with a six character filename and .DA extension.  You will need to 
know the number of lines in the file.  Lines may not be longer than
80 characters.  Then proceed as follows:
	Turn on VADIC modem and check wire to PDP-12.
	.R COM2  and give it filename and number of lines.
	Call CDC and login.
	COMMAND-ATTACH,LIB1
	COMMAND-LIBRARY,LIB1
	COMMAND-COM2
	Wait for message, then hit ^G to start transmission.  MQ
shows characters being transmitted.  Wait for end message.
	COMMAND-CATALOG,TAPE7,filename
	Logout, and hit ^C to terminate PDP-12 program.

III.  CDC to PDP-12 communication uses the COM3 programs.  The file 
to be transmitted must be on TAPE4, and only 80 characters per line
can be transmitted.  At the PDP-12, the file will be written on DTA1:
with your specified six character filename and .DA extension.
Proceed as follows:
	Turn modem on.
	.AS DSK DTA1    (if you want file on DSK:)
	.R COM3  and give it output filename.
	Login on CDC.
	COMMAND-ATTACH,LIB1
	COMMAND-LIBRARY,LIB1
	COMMAND-ETL,60   (time limit, for big files)
	COMMAND-ATTACH,TAPE4,filename
	COMMAND-COM3
	Wait for message, then hit ^G to proceed.  After each 100 
100 lines is received a message is printed and errors are indicated.
	Logout, hit ^G to terminate PDP-12 program.
